## 5. Decision Tree Classifier

### How it works
Works like a 20 questions game — asks a series of yes/no questions to reach a conclusion:

```
Is Sex == female?
    ├── Yes → Is Pclass == 1?
    │           ├── Yes → SURVIVED ✅
    │           └── No  → Did NOT survive ❌
    └── No  → Is Age < 10?
                ├── Yes → SURVIVED ✅
                └── No  → Did NOT survive ❌
```

The model learns WHICH questions to ask and in WHAT order — purely from training data.

### Code
```python
from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier

model = DecisionTreeClassifier(random_state=42)
model.fit(X_train, y_train)  # learning happens here
print("✅ Model trained!")
```

