## 9. Feature Importance — EDA

Always explore your data BEFORE building a model.

```python
# Survival rate by Sex
print(df.groupby('Sex')['Survived'].mean())
# male   → 0.19 (19% survived)
# female → 0.74 (74% survived)

# Survival rate by Pclass
print(df.groupby('Pclass')['Survived'].mean())
# 1st class → 0.63
# 2nd class → 0.47
# 3rd class → 0.24

# Survival rate by Age group
df['AgeGroup'] = pd.cut(df['Age'], bins=[0,12,18,60,100],
                         labels=['Child','Teen','Adult','Senior'])
print(df.groupby('AgeGroup')['Survived'].mean())
```

**Titanic findings:**
- **Sex** — most important feature (74% females vs 19% males survived)
- **Pclass** — second most important (rich = closer to lifeboats)
- **Age** — children prioritized

> **Rule:** Data always tells a story. Read it before modeling.

