## 11. Common Errors & Fixes

### KeyError — Column not found
```python
# ❌ WRONG — Fare dropped on line 1, accessed on line 2
df = df[['Survived', 'Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age']]  # Fare dropped here
X = df[['Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age', 'Fare']]        # KeyError!

# ✅ FIX — include all columns you need upfront
df = df[['Survived', 'Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age', 'Fare']]  # keep Fare
X = df[['Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age', 'Fare']]                # works!
```

### ValueError — Feature mismatch during prediction
```python
# ❌ WRONG — trained with 4 features, predicting with 3
model.fit(X_train, y_train)  # trained on Pclass, Sex, Age, Fare
new = pd.DataFrame([[1, 1, 25]], columns=['Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age'])
model.predict(new)  # ValueError — Fare is missing!

# ✅ FIX — prediction must have exact same columns as training
new = pd.DataFrame([[1, 1, 25, 500]], columns=['Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age', 'Fare'])
model.predict(new)  # works!
```

### Jupyter Memory Error
```python
# Problem — old variables stay in memory even after deleting cells
# Fix — always reload data at top of cell

url = "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/..."
df = pd.read_csv(url)  # ← always reload fresh

# OR go to: Kernel → Restart & Run All
```

> **Golden Rule:** Weird error that doesn't match your code?
> **Restart Kernel and Run All.** Fixes 90% of Jupyter issues.

