## Interview Tips — Day 3

**Q: What is overfitting and how do you prevent it?**
> *"Overfitting is when a model memorizes training data instead of learning patterns.
> It scores high on training data but poorly on new data.
> Prevention: always split data into separate train and test sets,
> use cross-validation, or simplify the model."*

**Q: Walk me through building an ML model from scratch.**
> 1. Load and explore the data
> 2. Clean and prepare — handle missing values, encode categories
> 3. Split into train and test sets
> 4. Train the model with `model.fit(X_train, y_train)`
> 5. Evaluate with `accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)`

**Q: How would you improve a model with 75% accuracy?**
> 1. Add more relevant features
> 2. Try a better algorithm (Random Forest, XGBoost)
> 3. Get more/better quality training data
> 4. Question if higher accuracy is even realistic for this dataset

